# Component styles

A styled component is a folder: `index.tsx` plus `styles.module.css`. Do not put a named CSS module next to a named component file.

## Do

```
search/bar/
  index.tsx
  styles.module.css
  typeahead/
    index.tsx
    styles.module.css
```

```tsx
import styles from "./styles.module.css";
```

## Don't

```
search/bar/lib/
  typeahead.tsx
  typeahead.module.css
```

```tsx
import styles from "./typeahead.module.css";
```

## Details

- One CSS module per component folder, always named `styles.module.css`.
- CSS-less helpers (`editor-state.ts`, plugins, data) stay as named files.
- Sibling files that share styles belong in one folder and import that folder's `styles.module.css`. Do not add `foo.module.css` beside `foo.tsx`.
- Import the folder (`./typeahead`, `@/components/search/bar/lib/help`). Do not import `styles.module.css` from another component.
- A large or multi-section CSS file means the TSX should split. Extract the sub-UI into its own folder and take the CSS with it. Never carve CSS into partials while leaving one god-component.
